:"யானை","lemma":"யானை","gloss":"elephant"}],"gloss":"elephant"},{"surface":"கலிமான்","parts":[{"text":"கலி","lemma":"கலி","gloss":"spirited"},{"text":"மான்","lemma":"மான்","gloss":"horse"}],"gloss":"spirited horses"},{"surface":"பேக","parts":[{"text":"பேக","lemma":"பேகன்","gloss":"O Began"}],"gloss":"O Began"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"பசித்தும்","parts":[{"text":"பசித்தும்","lemma":"பசி","gloss":"even being hungry"}],"gloss":"even being hungry"},{"surface":"வாரோம்","parts":[{"text":"வாரோம்","lemma":"வா","gloss":"we do not come"}],"gloss":"we do not come"},{"surface":"பாரமும்","parts":[{"text":"பாரம்","lemma":"பாரம்","gloss":"dependents"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"உம்","gloss":"and"}],"gloss":"and dependents"},{"surface":"இலமே","parts":[{"text":"இலம்","lemma":"இல்","gloss":"we do not have"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"indeed"}],"gloss":"we do not have indeed"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"களங்கனி","parts":[{"text":"களம்","lemma":"களவி","gloss":"kalavu plant"},{"text":"கனி","lemma":"கனி","gloss":"fruit"}],"gloss":"black kalavu fruit"},{"surface":"அன்ன","parts":[{"text":"அன்ன","lemma":"அன்ன","gloss":"like"}],"gloss":"like"},{"surface":"கருங்கோட்டு","parts":[{"text":"கருங்கோட்டு","lemma":"கருங்கோட்டு","gloss":"black-stemmed"}],"gloss":"black-stemmed","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"சீறியாழ்","parts":[{"text":"சீறியாழ்","lemma":"சீறியாழ்","gloss":"small lute"}],"gloss":"small lute","split_unverified":true}]},{"words":[{"surface":"நயம்","parts":[{"text":"நயம்","lemma":"நயம்","gloss":"melody"}],"gloss":"melody"},{"surface":"புரிந்து","parts":[{"text":"புரிந்து","lemma":"புரி","gloss":"desiring"}],"gloss":"desiring"},{"surface":"உறையுநர்","parts":[{"text":"உறையுநர்","lemma":"உறை","gloss":"those who play"}],"gloss":"those who play"},{"surface":"நடுங்க","parts":[{"text":"நடுங்க","lemma":"நடுங்கு","gloss":"to vibrate"}],"gloss":"to vibrate"},{"surface":"பண்ணி","parts":[{"text":"பண்ணி","lemma":"பண்","gloss":"having tuned"}],"gloss":"having tuned"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"அறம்","parts":[{"text":"அறம்","lemma":"அறம்","gloss":"righteousness"}],"gloss":"righteousness"},{"surface":"செய்தீமோ","parts":[{"text":"செய்","lemma":"செய்","gloss":"do"},{"text":"தீமோ","lemma":"தீமோ","gloss":"imperative suffix"}],"gloss":"please do"},{"surface":"அருள்","parts":[{"text":"அருள்","lemma":"அருள்","gloss":"grace"}],"gloss":"grace"},{"surface":"வெய்யோய்","parts":[{"text":"வெய்யோய்","lemma":"வெய்","gloss":"you who desire"}],"gloss":"O you who desire"},{"surface":"என","parts":[{"text":"என","lemma":"என","gloss":"saying"}],"gloss":"saying"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"இ·தியாம்","parts":[{"text":"இ·தியாம்","lemma":"இ·தியாம்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"இரந்த","parts":[{"text":"இரந்த","lemma":"இரந்த","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"பரிசில்","parts":[{"text":"பரிசில்","lemma":"பரிசில்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"அ·து","parts":[{"text":"அ·து","lemma":"அ·து","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"இருளின்","parts":[{"text":"இருளின்","lemma":"இருளின்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true}],"as_printed":true},{"words":[{"surface":"இனமணி","parts":[{"text":"இனம்","lemma":"இனம்","gloss":"group"},{"text":"மணி","lemma":"மணி","gloss":"bells"}],"gloss":"grouped bells"},{"surface":"நெடுந்தேர்","parts":[{"text":"நெடுந்தேர்","lemma":"நெடுந்தேர்","gloss":"tall chariot"}],"gloss":"tall chariot","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"ஏறி","parts":[{"text":"ஏறி","lemma":"ஏறு","gloss":"having mounted"}],"gloss":"having mounted"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"இன்னாது","parts":[{"text":"இன்னாது","lemma":"இன்னாது","gloss":"painfully"}],"gloss":"painfully"},{"surface":"உறைவி","parts":[{"text":"உறைவி","lemma":"உறை","gloss":"she who dwells"}],"gloss":"she who dwells"},{"surface":"அரும்படர்","parts":[{"text":"அரும்","lemma":"அருமை","gloss":"deep"},{"text":"படர்","lemma":"படர்","gloss":"grief"}],"gloss":"deep grief"},{"surface":"களைமே","parts":[{"text":"களை","lemma":"களை","gloss":"remove"},{"text":"மே","lemma":"மே","gloss":"imperative particle"}],"gloss":"please remove"}]}],"literal":"Soft-natured dark peacock will shiver, thinking so, having pitied / and given a shawl, O Began of undying good fame, / rutting elephant, and spirited horses! / Even being hungry we do not come, and we do not have dependents indeed. / Like the black kalavu fruit, the black-stemmed small lute, / making those who play desiring melody vibrate, having tuned, / 'Please do righteousness, O you who desire grace!' saying, / this is the gift we requested; that is, in the darkness, / mounting the tall chariot with grouped bells, / please remove the deep grief of her who dwells painfully.","translation":"O Began of undying fame, who possesses rutting elephants and spirited horses, you who once pitied a soft-natured dark peacock thinking it was shivering and wrapped it in your shawl! We do not come to you out of hunger, nor do we have a burden of dependents. Tuning our small lute with its black stem resembling the dark kalavu fruit, making its sweet melody vibrate, we sing: 'O you who love to show grace, do what is righteous!' This is the only gift we beg of you: mount your tall chariot with its ringing bells, and go in the dark of night to remove the deep grief of your wife who lives in painful solitude.","modern":"மென்மையான இயல்புடைய கரிய மயில் குளிரால் நடுங்கும் என்று இரக்கப்பட்டு அதற்குப் போர்வையை அளித்த, அழியாத நல்ல புகழையும், மதயானைகளையும், கலிமா குதிரைகளையும் உடைய பேகனே! நாங்கள் பசியோடு வரவில்லை; எங்களுக்குச் சுற்றத்தாராகிய பாரமும் இல்லை. களாப்பழம் போன்ற கரிய தண்டினைக் கொண்ட சிறிய யாழில் இனிய இசையை விரும்பி வாசிப்பவர் நடுங்கும்படி பண்ணி, 'அருளை விரும்பும் வள்ளலே! அறத்தைச் செய்வாயாக!' என்று பாடினோம். யாம் உன்னிடம் இரந்து கேட்கும் பரிசு இதுவே: இந்த இருள் நிறைந்த இரவிலே, கூட்டமாகிய மணிகளைக் கட்டிய நெடிய தேரில் ஏறிச் சென்று, உன்னைப் பிரிந்து துன்பத்துடன் வாழும் உன் மனைவியின் அரிய துயரத்தைப் போக்குவாயாக!","explanation":"This poem is addressed to the chieftain Vēḷ Pēkaṉ by the poet Kapilar. Pēkaṉ was famous for his extraordinary generosity, famously giving his expensive shawl to a peacock thinking it was shivering from the cold. However, he had abandoned his wife, Kaṇṇaki, and was living with another woman. Kapilar, along with other poets, visited Pēkaṉ not to beg for wealth or food, but to urge him to return to his grieving wife. The poet tunes his small lute (cīṟiyāḻ) and sings that the only gift (paricil) they desire from him is for him to mount his chariot and go back to his wife to relieve her deep sorrow (arumpaṭar). This poem belongs to the Peruintiṇai category as it deals with mismatched or improper love/separation, specifically the poet's intervention in a domestic crisis.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"}}